# Production collection distribution policy (issue #360).
#
# Checked-in, non-secret target topology for the air-gapped deployment:
# 6 logical shards, 3 copies of every shard across the three Qdrant peers,
# 2 required write acknowledgements. Applied to the corpus collection and
# its paired completion/control collection. Rationale, failure contract and
# migration rules live in docs/deploy.md#collection-policy.
#
# Consumed by scripts/airgap/common.sh as the lowest-precedence default:
# an explicit caller environment value wins, then the operator airgap.env,
# then this fragment. One-node / local / CI lanes select 1/1/1 explicitly;
# never infer a downgrade from the available node count. An explicitly
# cleared key in the operator file disables the preset and fails the
# complete-tuple validation instead of silently qualifying production.
QDRANT_SHARD_NUMBER=6
QDRANT_REPLICATION_FACTOR=3
QDRANT_WRITE_CONSISTENCY_FACTOR=2
